152:## 5. Derivation rules the schema must support
153-
154-These belong to the derivation engine, but the schema is shaped to make them
155-expressible, and each is a place where a naive model would produce wrong figures.
156-
157-1. Balls faced counts deliveries where no wide was bowled. A no-ball is faced; a
158-   wide is not.
159-2. Runs conceded by a bowler include wides and no-balls but exclude byes and
160-   leg-byes.
161-3. Boundaries count four or six off the bat, excluding the 232 deliveries flagged
162-   `non_boundary`, where the runs were run rather than struck to the rope.
163-4. A team total is the sum of delivery totals **plus** innings-level penalty runs
164-   (O7).
165-5. Legal balls in an over must be counted, never assumed to be six (O6).
166-6. Career aggregates group by person identifier, never by name (O2).
167-7. A wicket is credited to the bowler only for those dismissal kinds flagged
168-   `credits_bowler`. A run out is not the bowler's wicket.
169-8. Super-over innings are excluded from standard aggregates by default.
