173-## 6. Deferred entities
174-
175-`database/schema/event-model.md` identifies four further concerns that this
176-iteration does not implement: validation and review state; statistic definitions
177-and their versions; derived statistic results and their provenance; and dataset
178-releases and export jobs.
179-
180-They are deferred deliberately, not overlooked. A derived result cannot be
181-modelled before the events it derives from exist, and a statistic definition
182-cannot be versioned before the derivation engine establishes what a definition
183-contains. Their intended shape:
184-
185-- **Validation state** belongs on `submission`, which already carries a status.
186-  A richer review workflow — who reviewed, when, against which rule — extends that
187-  table rather than replacing it.
188-- **Statistic definition and version** requires a definition identifier, a version,
189-  and the expression or code reference that computes it, so that a published
190-  figure can name the version that produced it. The super-over exclusion in rule 8
191-  belongs here rather than in query code.
192-- **Derived result** requires the definition version, the scope computed over, the
193-  value, and the deliveries consumed, so that a correction can identify which
194-  results are now stale.
195-- **Dataset release** requires a release identifier, the scope, the point in time
196-  represented, and a manifest, so that a consumer holding an older reference can
197-  still resolve it.
198-
199-What must be settled first: which statistics the client actually requires, which
200-is the subject of #37, and how a release identifies the state of the data at a
201-point in time.
